{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}
Down in the [G]valley, the valley so [D]low,
Hang your head over, hear the wind [G]blow.
Hear the wind blow, dear, hear the wind [D]blow;
Hang your head over, hear the wind [G]blow.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}
Roses love [G]sunshine, violets love [D]dew,
Angels in heaven know I love [G]you.
Know I love you, dear, know I love [D]you;
Angels in heaven know I love [G]you.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 3"}
Writing this [G]letter, containing three [D]lines,
Answer my question: will you be [G]mine?
Will you be mine, dear, will you be [D]mine?
Answer my question: will you be [G]mine?
{end_of_verse}
{x_end: G}
